    add('Representative failures expose different layers. A deterioration draft can correctly observe low oxygen saturation yet wrongly call ordinary indicators red flags; source traceability cannot rescue that inference. A CRP discussion can correctly reject a single-test decision while inventing a testing interval absent from the retrieved guidance. Auditors also make errors: in one deterioration review, both treated the treatment framework as requiring a red flag, overlooking its alternative of two or more non-red-flag factors or indicators. An incomplete stopping case can omit a conjunctive criterion despite a genuine citation. Missing-result cases can drift into reassurance. Withholding reduces answer availability, and auditor agreement alone does not resolve shared interpretive errors.')
    add('Latency is not reported as a model-quality result because archived operational timings mix provider waits, new calls and replayed steps. The CPU container\'s no-network, read-only, non-root startup/authentication smoke test passed, and cached MiniLM weights completed the offline retrieval evaluation. The final application still requires hosted end-to-end checks after its database and reviewed corpus are provisioned.')
    add('## 8. Discussion and limitations')
    add('The experiments illustrate why model discrimination, evidence retrieval, generation quality and release safety require separate claims. A classifier can nearly reproduce a supplied label while the data remain unsuitable for the intended clinical forecast. A retrieved quote can be authentic while the generated sentence misstates its meaning. A verification gate can reduce emitted unsupported content by withholding almost everything, without producing a useful answer. Reporting the label definition, all-case metrics and release coverage makes these distinctions visible.')
    add('The supplied CSV has unresolved identity, unit, provenance and outcome defects. Patient-ID isolation mitigates direct grouping leakage but cannot repair incorrect grouping or guarantee that related records represent distinct people. The secondary age subset is not an external cohort. Availability timestamps are absent, so forecasting lead time and early-warning benefit cannot be computed. The study does not compare a clinically validated EOS calculator with the research classifier, and the previously used hand-built point score is not presented as an accepted clinical baseline.')
    add('The RAG fixture is small, synthetic, English-language and based on one guideline extraction. References were written by the engineering workflow, and repeated variants share templates. The same cases informed the quote-ID refinement, preventing an untouched-test interpretation. The graph ablation uses deterministic concept expansion without a live graph database, and the dense experiment uses exact similarity without a deployed vector service. These controlled measurements inform engineering choices but do not establish production retrieval coverage across all neonatal subpopulations or institutions.')
    add('No clinician review of generated care plans, clinical validation, prospective deployment study or clinical usability study was performed; this work reports supplied-label modeling and synthetic engineering evaluation only.')
    add('A subsequent study should establish a culture-adjudicated cohort with true birth/onset/availability times; compare snapshot and causal longitudinal predictors; test calibration across sites and prevalence shifts; create independently authored cases and reference answers; evaluate graph relations and source scope; and assess abstention, omissions and workflow fit under realistic workloads. Different model families for auditing and judging would help investigate shared-error dependence, but would not by themselves establish correctness. An actual clinical release requires evidence outside the scope of this development benchmark.')
    add('## 9. Conclusion')
    add('NeoGuard EOS provides an implemented architecture for joining serial observed findings to statistical models and source-linked explanations while preserving separate eligibility and release boundaries. Actual experiments train calibrated classifiers on the supplied neonatal labels and expose serious source-data limitations. Synthetic experiments quantify retrieval differences and the cost of complete-plan verification, including service failure, abstention and unsupported inferences. Immutable quote IDs improve citation mechanics; concept expansion does not improve this benchmark. The resulting artifacts support reproducible research and further refinement while keeping unsupported EOS and deployment claims out of the application.')
    add('## 10. Reproducibility and artifact availability')
