    add('Each negative control independently shuffles fit and test labels for three fixed seeds; the resulting AUC ranges are descriptive, not a permutation significance test. Scores of the same random fits against the original labels are also retained, including non-chance values; they are not substituted for the negative-control result. Standardized nearest-neighbor checks on 1,000 sampled test rows per cohort found no effectively identical fit rows, but are not exhaustive. Strong laboratory-only separation and high discrimination after removing CRP/PCT leave the source-label construction question unresolved. Deliberate 1,000-fold unit errors can preserve high AUC, demonstrating why discrimination cannot validate an input mapping. The serving boundary rejects invalid scales and values outside fit support.')
    add('### 11.2 Four-estimator comparison and SHAP')
